      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weighting is similar to an integral, where the Fourier Transform integrates the area under the wave curve, taking into account the decay of amplitude with frequency. This helps to overlook the high-frequency noise and focus on the lower-frequency components. The sorting happens through a process called abscissa mapping, where the frequencies get 'sorted' based on their value (usually expressed in radians per time), and the resulting coefficients (sines and cosines) output the specific amplitudes and phases of each frequency component.",
